          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How to manage construction worker payroll in Delhi?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Attendance-based at Delhi min wage (VDA half-yearly). PF/ESI mandatory (ESI even for 1 worker - hazardous). BOCW registration for 10+ workers. Patron manages from Rohini office."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is ESI mandatory for construction workers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Construction = hazardous under Labour Codes. ESI mandatory for even 1 employee (not the general 10-threshold). 0.75% employee + 3.25% employer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the construction payroll cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Rs 50/employee/month (100+ workers). Rs 75 (smaller sites). PF/ESI filing included. BOCW support Rs 5K-10K one-time. Multi-site NCR Rs 3K-8K/month add-on."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is Delhi minimum wage for construction?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Category-specific: unskilled/semi-skilled/skilled/highly skilled. Revised half-yearly (April + October) via VDA. Patron updates rates same day as notification."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is BOCW cess?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "1% of construction cost. Paid to Delhi BOCW Welfare Board. Funds worker welfare (pension, medical, education). Must register for 10+ workers. Non-payment = prosecution."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can Delhi builders run NCR multi-site payroll?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes but 3 different state regimes. Delhi/Haryana/UP each have separate min wages and labour rules. Workers moving between sites need split calculations. Patron tracks separately."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What if sub-contractor doesn't deposit PF/ESI?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Principal employer (builder) becomes liable under EPF and ESI Acts. EPFO/ESIC recover from builder with interest + penalties. Patron monitors sub-contractors monthly."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How fast is setup?",
