<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Construction Payroll in Delhi: BOCW, PF/ESI, and Site Worker Compliance</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Construction Payroll in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>Construction payroll = site worker salary (Delhi min wage + VDA half-yearly) + PF 12%+12% + ESI mandatory even for 1 worker (hazardous) + BOCW 1% cess + contract labour monitoring + S.194C TDS on contractors + multi-site NCR (Delhi/Haryana/UP = 3 different regimes) + RERA project cost allocation + 50% basic rule (Labour Codes Nov 2025). From Rs 50/employee/month. Patron Rohini office.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi's construction sector is one of India's largest. For a comprehensive overview, see our <a href="/payroll-services-for-construction-real-estate-industry">Construction Payroll</a> national guide.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Governing Acts</td><td>BOCW 1996, EPF 1952, ESI 1948, Contract Labour 1970, Payment of Wages, Labour Codes 2025, RERA</td></tr><tr><td>Key Rates</td><td>PF 12%+12%. ESI 0.75%+3.25% (mandatory - hazardous). BOCW 1% construction cost</td></tr><tr><td>Cost From</td><td>Rs 50/employee/month (100+); Rs 75/employee (smaller sites)</td></tr><tr><td>Penalty</td><td>PF default up to Rs 3L + imprisonment. ESI similar. BOCW non-registration = prosecution</td></tr><tr><td>Delhi</td><td>No PT. VDA revised half-yearly. BOCW Welfare Board. EPFO/ESIC Delhi</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p</p>
                <p>DDA residential (Dwarka/Rohini/Narela), Aerocity/Saket commercial, Pragati Maidan redevelopment, Delhi Metro extensions. Hundreds of thousands of workers. BOCW Act for 10+ workers. Construction = hazardous = ESI for even 1 employee. VDA half-yearly. NCR = 3 state regimes. 50% basic rule now in effect. Patron Rohini office handles EPFO/ESIC/BOCW Delhi.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Construction Payroll?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Definition:</strong> Specialised salary processing for site workers, supervisors, engineers, and contract labour in construction - governed by BOCW Act, EPF, ESI, Contract Labour Act, Payment of Wages, new Labour Codes, and RERA.</p><p><strong>Delhi complexity:</strong> Transient workforce, multi-tiered employer chains (builder→contractor→sub-contractor), hazardous ESI, VDA half-yearly, 3-state NCR compliance, RERA project allocation.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> Dwarka builder with 200 workers across 3 sub-contractors: every worker needs UAN + ESIC IP + Delhi minimum wage + BOCW cess 1% deposited.</p><p>See <a href="/payroll-processing-and-management-services">Payroll Services</a> for general payroll.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Construction Payroll in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>BOCW Act 1996:</strong> 10+ construction workers = mandatory registration. 1% cess on construction cost to Delhi BOCW Welfare Board. Worker welfare schemes.</p><p><strong>Hazardous Work:</strong> Construction = hazardous under Labour Codes. ESI mandatory for even 1 employee (not the general 10-employee threshold).</p><p><strong>Contract Labour Act 1970:</strong> Principal employer liable if contractor defaults on PF/ESI/wages. Must monitor sub-contractor compliance.</p><p><strong>VDA:</strong> Variable Dearness Allowance. Delhi construction minimum wages revised April + October per CPI.</p><p><strong>50% Basic Rule:</strong> Labour Codes Nov 2025. Basic ≥50% of CTC. Increases PF/ESI base. 15-25% cost increase for non-compliant structures.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
